    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "I1 not met. Study uses drug WORDS (semantic/linguistic cues) presented on screen, not visual drug images. The review objective specifies 'using visual stimuli,' where in neuroimaging literature 'visual drug cues' refers to images/pictures of drugs or drug paraphernalia, not verbal/semantic cues like words. Study qualifies on other criteria but fails on the core cue modality requirement."
   },
   {
